+# Correcting a Booked Visit Is In Scope; Cancelling One Stays Out
+
+**Status:** Accepted
+
+## Context
+
+NG-5 was confirmed deliberate on 2026-08-08 as "Changing or cancelling a visit once booked," and [that ADR](2026-08-08-non-goal-deletion-and-visit-amendment.md) recorded that narrowing the row later is a separate owner decision carrying its own non-goal ADR. The owner has now made that decision (2026-08-27): correcting a booked visit's date and description should be available, while cancelling a booked visit should not.
+
+## Options Considered
+
+1. **Leave NG-5 whole.** Keep both changing and cancelling out. Rejected: the owner has decided correction is worth showing — forward correction of a visit matches the correction flows already demonstrated for owner and pet details.
+2. **Open the whole row.** Add both correction and cancellation. Rejected: cancellation introduces visit lifecycle and retirement state the sample carries nowhere; the create and update flows already teach what correction demonstrates.
+3. **Narrow NG-5 to cancellation only** (chosen). Correction moves into scope; cancellation remains the standing non-goal.
+
+## Decision
+
+Correcting a booked visit's date and description is in scope, recorded as `REQ-VIS-003`. Cancelling or withdrawing a booked visit remains out of scope; NG-5 now names cancellation alone. Correction updates the visit in place — it never removes a visit and never adds one.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- NG-5 shrinks to "Cancelling a visit once booked"; the sample now demonstrates forward correction of a visit alongside owner and pet correction.
+- The visit remains free of retirement or lifecycle state — there is still no path to remove a booked visit.
+- A later request to add cancellation reopens NG-5 only on an explicit owner decision with its own non-goal ADR, per the convention the 2026-08-08 ADR set.
+
+## Implementation
+
+**Non-goal:** NG-5
+
+- [PRD Non-Goals](../prd.md#non-goals) — the narrowed NG-5 row.
+- [PRD Visits, REQ-VIS-003](../prd.md#req-vis-003) — the correction capability now in scope.
